  "narrative": "All twelve new discovery comparisons had valid Welch cells and are interpreted on the signed scale already aligned to each registered hypothesis direction. A positive signed estimate supports the claimed direction, and the 0.15 composite dependency-score-unit threshold is applied to the signed lower bound. The central new finding is threshold-exceeding assay-tail heterogeneity of the accepted feature_010 association. H100 tests the high feature_038 tail interaction in the claimed attenuation direction: signed estimate +0.590, 95% CI +0.338 to +0.842. Because H100 has direction -1, positive signed evidence corresponds to a raw interaction of approximately -0.590, meaning the feature_010=1 higher-outcome contrast is attenuated in the feature_038 >= 1 tail relative to its complement. The lower bound is well above 0.15, so I accept H100 as a dataset-internal effect-modification claim, but I keep it active and request independent validation because it directly tests the central feature_010 high-tail attenuation pattern and interaction estimates are more vulnerable to discovery-sample overprecision than the accepted main effects. H101 similarly supports threshold-exceeding enhancement of feature_010 in the low feature_038 tail: signed +0.571, CI +0.398 to +0.744. I accept and close H101; with H92's high-tail mean rejection and H93's low-tail mean acceptance, this gives a coherent descriptive pattern rather than evidence of causality or mechanism.\n\nThe feature_018 tail analyses show a comparable pattern for feature_010. H96, the mean feature_010 effect in feature_018 >= 1 in the claimed higher-outcome direction, is not supported: signed -0.224, CI -0.495 to +0.047. The point estimate is actually in the opposite raw direction, so I reject and close H96. H97, the mean feature_010 effect in feature_018 <= -1, is very strong: signed +0.803, CI +0.645 to +0.960, so H97 is accepted. The direct interactions make this attenuation/enhancement more than a pair of separate tail means: H104, in the high feature_018 attenuation direction, gives signed +0.780, CI +0.492 to +1.067, and H105, in the low feature_018 enhancement direction, gives signed +0.449, CI +0.258 to +0.640. All three lower bounds are far above 0.15, so I accept H104 and H105 and close them. Again, these are dataset-internal association patterns across standardized assay tails, not claims that feature_018 causes feature_010 to behave differently or that the pattern generalizes.\n\nThe accepted feature_037 and feature_002 associations remain broadly robust in feature_018 tails. For feature_037, direction -1, H94 gives signed +0.966 with CI +0.796 to +1.137 in feature_018 >= 1, and H95 gives signed +0.588 with CI +0.427 to +0.750 in feature_018 <= -1. Both lower bounds exceed threshold, so both are accepted and closed. For feature_002, direction +1, H102 gives signed +0.960 with CI +0.806 to +1.114 in feature_018 >= 1, and H103 gives signed +0.653 with CI +0.489 to +0.817 in feature_018 <= -1. Both lower bounds exceed threshold, so both are accepted and closed. Thus feature_018 tails delimit exact subgroup claims for feature_010, whereas feature_037 and feature_002 retain large associations in both tails.\n\nH37 and H38 test the feature_010 mean association in feature_036 tails. Feature_010 remains significantly higher-outcome in feature_036 <= -0.5 by +0.393, CI +0.224 to +0.562, and in feature_036 >= 0.5 by +0.473, CI +0.279 to +0.667. Both lower bounds exceed 0.15, so both are accepted and closed. Unlike the feature_038 and feature_018 extremes, feature_036 tails do not reveal a feature_010 reversal or attenuation in these observed tail means. Overall, the new evidence preserves the three accepted central axes and refines the picture: feature_010 is the only central axis showing strong, threshold-exceeding association heterogeneity across standardized assay tails. I request validation only for H100 because it is the central high-feature_038 attenuation interaction; the remaining new claims have discovery lower bounds comfortably above the threshold and do not currently justify additional validation spending.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 7 appraise update.\n\nCentral validated axes remain:\n- feature_037=1 -> stronger dependency/lower outcome_001 (H19 accepted/closed/validated; robust across feature_002, feature_010, clinical feature_040, age feature_019, feature_038 tails, and feature_018 tails).\n- feature_010=1 -> weaker dependency/higher outcome_001 (H34 accepted/closed/validated overall; robust conditional on feature_002, feature_037, feature_040, feature_019, feature_036 tail means, and feature_018 low tail).\n- feature_002=1 -> weaker dependency/higher outcome_001 (H70 accepted/closed/validated overall; robust across feature_037, feature_010, feature_040, feature_019, feature_038 tails, and feature_018 tails).\n\nMajor new structure: feature_010 assay-tail heterogeneity is now supported at threshold by direct interactions, not only separate tail means.\n- feature_038 >= 1: H92 high-tail mean rejected; H100 high-tail attenuation interaction accepted but active pending independent validation. Discovery H100 signed +0.590 CI +0.338 to +0.842, direction -1; positive signed means raw attenuation.\n- feature_038 <= -1: H93 low-tail mean accepted; H101 low-tail enhancement interaction accepted/closed. H101 signed +0.571 CI +0.398 to +0.744.\n- feature_018 >= 1: H96 high-tail feature_010 mean rejected; H104 high-tail attenuation interaction accepted/closed. H104 signed +0.780 CI +0.492 to +1.067, direction -1.\n- feature_018 <= -1: H97 low-tail feature_010 mean accepted; H105 low-tail enhancement interaction accepted/closed. H105 signed +0.449 CI +0.258 to +0.640.\n- feature_036 tails: feature_010 means accepted in both H37 (+0.393 CI +0.224 to +0.562) and H38 (+0.473 CI +0.279 to +0.667), suggesting less extreme feature_036-tail heterogeneity than feature_038/feature_018, though direct feature_036 interaction tests are not yet registered/tested.\n\nRobust feature_018 tails for other central axes:\n- feature_037 accepted in feature_018 >= 1 (H94 +0.966 CI +0.796 to +1.137) and <= -1 (H95 +0.588 CI +0.427 to +0.750).\n- feature_002 accepted in feature_018 >= 1 (H102 +0.960 CI +0.806 to +1.114) and <= -1 (H103 +0.653 CI +0.489 to +0.817).\n\nCentral interaction status:\n- feature_002-by-feature_037 rejected/closed (R69).\n- feature_002-by-feature_010 rejected/closed after validation failure (R68/R76).\n- Direct feature_037-by-feature_010 interactions H45/H46 remain active but lower priority; cross-stratum mean effects are similar and feature_002 interactions are null.\n\nValidation request: H100. Reason: central direct interaction for the accepted feature_010 axis, testing high feature_038 attenuation. Discovery lower bound exceeds threshold, but interaction estimates and the original tail-mean pattern deserve independent reproduction. If validation supports H100, central feature_010 tail attenuation becomes more secure. If validation fails threshold, keep accepted feature_010 overall and tail-mean findings, but downgrade the exact high feature_038 interaction to unresolved/closed as appropriate.\n\nNext analysis priorities:\n1. Await H100 validation.\n2. Use remaining slots for registered untested lines: H106/H107 feature_002 feature_036 tail means; H35/H36 feature_037 feature_036 tails if needed; broad categorical screens H67/H68/H69/H82/H98/H99/H108/H109. Consider adding feature_010-by-feature_036 direct interaction tests if direct tail closure remains important after H100 validation.\n3. Do not validate every large accepted tail mean; reserve validation for borderline or central unresolved claims.\n\nInterpretation guardrails:\n- outcome_001 is composite dependency score, not gene knockout.\n- More negative outcome_001 means stronger dependency.\n- All accepted claims are dataset-internal associations; validation supports reproducibility within this data-generating process, not causality, mechanism, or transportability.\n- Interaction estimates are effect in subgroup minus effect in complement, already signed to proposal direction.",
