  "narrative": "Two due claims required reassessment. H70, the overall feature_002=1 association with weaker composite dependency/higher outcome_001, is strongly supported: discovery gave +0.832 units (95% CI +0.766 to +0.897), and independent validation gave +0.851 (independent interval +0.756 to +0.945), both far above the 0.15-unit threshold. I keep H70 accepted and closed as a dataset-internal association, not a causal or transportable claim.\n\nThe validation of H100 changes the strength of the exact feature_010 high-feature_038 attenuation interaction. Discovery gave a signed attenuation effect of +0.590 (CI +0.338 to +0.842), but independent validation gave only +0.360 with an independent interval from -0.036 to +0.756. The validation point estimate remains positive and above threshold, yet its lower bound does not exceed 0.15 and approaches the null. Thus the independent evidence is directionally consistent but not reproducible at the pre-specified threshold level. I therefore reassess H100 as unresolved rather than accepted. This does not reject the discovery signal or the accepted feature_010 main effect; it means the exact high-feature_038 interaction should not be reported as a robust validated threshold effect. One plausible explanation is that H100's complement includes the very strong low-feature_038 feature_010 effect, so the interaction may partly reflect low-tail enhancement rather than pure high-tail attenuation. I registered two sensitivity interactions that compare high-tail effects with ordinary values only, excluding low tails for feature_038 and feature_018. These are the most direct follow-up to the validation result.\n\nThe supported findings remain that outcome_001 in this supplied dataset is dominated by three separable measured axes: feature_037=1 is associated with stronger dependency/lower outcome_001; feature_010=1 is associated with weaker dependency/higher outcome_001; and feature_002=1 is associated with weaker dependency/higher outcome_001. Each main axis was validated with intervals well above threshold. Feature_037 and feature_010 remain strong conditional on feature_002, and feature_002 remains strong conditional on feature_037 and feature_010. The accepted feature_010 tail findings include a rejected/attenuated high feature_038 mean association, a very strong low feature_038 mean association, a low feature_038 enhancement interaction, and analogous low/high feature_018 associations and interactions. Feature_037 and feature_002 remain strong in feature_018 tails.\n\nImportant negative findings: the constructed binary research markers feature_007, feature_058, and feature_015 and their tail/interaction extensions do not support threshold associations; feature_003 is borderline below threshold in discovery and validation; the feature_002-by-feature_037 and feature_002-by-feature_010 interactions are not supported; and many common binary screens remain small. Unresolved evidence includes H100, the direct feature_037-by-feature_010 interactions, deferred feature_036 tails for feature_037, and many untested broad categorical screens. The next most informative analyses are the newly proposed high-tail ordinary-only sensitivity interactions, followed by the remaining broad categorical screens and registered feature_002 feature_036 tail means. All claims are dataset associations; none establishes biological mechanism, causality, or generalizability.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 7 synthesis update.\n\nDue assessments:\n- H70 accepted/closed/validated: feature_002=1 -> weaker dependency/higher outcome_001. Discovery +0.832 CI +0.766 to +0.897; validation +0.851 independent interval +0.756 to +0.945. Dataset association only.\n- H100 reassessed unresolved/active: high feature_038 feature_010 attenuation interaction. Discovery +0.590 CI +0.338 to +0.842. Validation +0.360 independent interval -0.036 to +0.756. Direction consistent but validation lower bound below 0.15 and near null. Do not present as robust validated threshold interaction.\n\nCurrent supported central axes:\n- feature_037=1 -> stronger dependency/lower outcome_001, validated; robust in feature_002, feature_010, feature_040, feature_019, feature_038 tails, feature_018 tails.\n- feature_010=1 -> weaker dependency/higher outcome_001, validated overall; robust in feature_002 and feature_037 conditionals, feature_040, feature_019, feature_036 tail means, low feature_038/low feature_018 tails.\n- feature_002=1 -> weaker dependency/higher outcome_001, validated; robust across many strata including feature_037/feature_010 conditionals and feature_018 tails.\n\nAccepted feature_010 tail structure (discovery-based unless noted):\n- feature_038 high mean rejected/null/opposite; feature_038 low mean accepted; feature_038 low interaction accepted.\n- feature_018 high mean rejected/opposite; feature_018 high interaction accepted; feature_018 low mean accepted; feature_018 low interaction accepted.\n- feature_036 tail means accepted both tails.\n- high feature_038 direct interaction now unresolved after validation; high feature_018 direct interaction remains accepted but unvalidated.\n\nNull/unsupported lines:\n- feature_007/feature_058/feature_015 markers and tails/interactions.\n- feature_003 borderline below threshold in discovery and validation.\n- feature_002-by-feature_037 and feature_002-by-feature_010 interactions.\n- Many common binary screens and nominal screens so far.\n\nMost informative next analysis:\n1. Newly registered high-tail sensitivity interactions excluding low tails: feature_010 high feature_038 vs ordinary feature_038 only, and feature_010 high feature_018 vs ordinary feature_018 only. These distinguish pure high-tail attenuation from interactions driven by low-tail enhancement.\n2. Then broad untested categorical screens and H106/H107 feature_002 feature_036 tails.\n\nValidation budget: remaining new requests reduced to 4. Reserve for new threshold-exceeding main effects or central unresolved interactions, not every accepted tail mean. Cached H100 validation should not be requested again.\n\nInterpretation guardrails:\n- outcome_001 composite dependency score, not gene knockout.\n- More negative outcome_001 means stronger dependency.\n- Accepted associations are dataset-internal; validation supports reproducibility, not causality, mechanism, or generalizability.\n- Interaction estimates are effect in subgroup minus effect in complement, already signed to proposal direction."
}
